      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "1. The volume of a pyramid is given by the formula: \\( V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{Base area} \\times \\text{Height} \\).\n2. For the original pyramid with a base edge of 12 cm and an altitude of 8 cm, the volume \\( V_{\\text{original}} \\) is:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\left(12 \\times 12\\right) \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3\n   \\]\n3. The volume of the smaller pyramid with a base edge of 6 cm and an altitude of 4 cm, \\( V_{\\text{small}} \\), is:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{small}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\left(6 \\times 6\\right) \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3\n   \\]\n4. The volume of the frustum is the difference between the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{small}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3\n   \\]\nSo, the volume of the frustum is \\(\\boxed{336}\\) cubic centimeters.\n```python\n# Calculation for the volume of the original pyramid\nbase_edge_original = 12\nheight_original = 8\nbase_area_original = base_edge_original ** 2\nvolume_original = (1/3) * base_area_original * height_original\n\n# Calculation for the volume of the smaller pyramid\nbase_edge_small = 6\nheight_small = 4\nbase_area_small = base_edge_small ** 2\nvolume_small = (1/3) * base_area_small * height_small\n\n# Calculation for the volume of the frustum\nvolume_frustum = volume_original - volume_small\nprint(volume_frustum)\n```",
